Monte Carlo sampling layer for GMM-based uncertainty propagation.
The user specifies a tolerance and confidence level, and sampling continues 
until the estimated confidence interval for the selected output quan-
tity satisfies the requested precision or the maximum sampling budget
is reached. The approach enables GMM-based uncertainty models to be
used in simulation-based planning, routing, inspection, and quality 
assessment in circular factories without manually fixing the Monte Carlo
sample size in advance. We demonstrate the workflow with a proof of
concept fatigue strength example for returned or treated metallic 
components. Multimodal surface state uncertainty is propagated through a
nonlinear fatigue strength relation and the output is assessed by its 
moments and by a low strength probability.",
